{"route":"/docs/6.0/guides/npm/","version":"6.0","renderedVersion":"6.0","title":{"id":"content","type":"heading","en":"Bootstrap and npm","level":1},"lead":{"id":"content--paragraph-1","type":"paragraph","en":"The official guide for how to build a starter project with Bootstrap’s CSS and JavaScript in your project using just npm."},"blocks":[{"id":"content--media-1","type":"media","html":"<img src=\"https://getbootstrap.com/docs/6.0/assets/img/guides/bootstrap-npm.png\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\">"},{"id":"content--note-1","type":"note","tone":"info","body":[{"id":"content--note-text-1","type":"note-text","en":"<strong>Want to skip to the end?</strong> Download the source code and working demo for this guide from the <a href=\"https://github.com/twbs/examples/tree/main/sass-js/\">twbs/examples repository</a>. You can also <a href=\"https://stackblitz.com/github/twbs/examples/tree/main/sass-js?file=index.html\">open the example in StackBlitz</a>."}]},{"id":"content--note-2","type":"note","tone":"info","body":[{"id":"content--note-text-2","type":"note-text","en":"<strong>Using an AI coding agent?</strong> Point it at our <a href=\"https://github.com/twbs/bootstrap/tree/main/skills/bootstrap-npm\"><code>bootstrap-npm</code> skill</a> to automate this setup. See <a href=\"https://getbootstrap.com/docs/6.0/getting-started/ai\">AI</a> for all available skills."}]},{"id":"what-is-npm","type":"heading","en":"What is npm?","level":2},{"id":"what-is-npm--paragraph-1","type":"paragraph","en":"<a href=\"https://www.npmjs.com/\">npm</a> is the default package manager for Node.js. In this guide, we use npm to install Bootstrap and its dependencies, then compile Sass to CSS using command-line tools—no bundler required."},{"id":"setup","type":"heading","en":"Setup","level":2},{"id":"setup--paragraph-1","type":"paragraph","en":"We’re building a npm project with Bootstrap from scratch, so there are some prerequisites and upfront steps before we get started. This guide requires you to have Node.js installed and some familiarity with the terminal."},{"id":"setup--list-1","type":"list","tag":"ol","items":[{"tag":"li","body":[{"id":"setup--item-1","type":"item","en":"<strong>Create a project folder and set up npm.</strong> We’ll create the <code>my-project</code> folder and initialize npm with the <code>-y</code> argument to avoid it asking us all the interactive questions."},{"id":"setup--code-1","type":"code","value":"mkdir my-project && cd my-project\nnpm init -y","language":""}]},{"tag":"li","body":[{"id":"setup--item-2","type":"item","en":"<strong>Install Bootstrap.</strong> Now we can install Bootstrap. We’ll also install Floating UI and Vanilla Calendar Pro since some of our components depend on them. If you don’t plan on using menus, popovers, or tooltips, you can omit Floating UI. If you don’t plan on using the datepicker, you can omit Vanilla Calendar Pro."},{"id":"setup--code-2","type":"code","value":"npm i --save bootstrap @floating-ui/dom vanilla-calendar-pro","language":""}]},{"tag":"li","body":[{"id":"setup--item-3","type":"item","en":"<strong>Install additional dependencies.</strong> In addition to Bootstrap, we need a few more dependencies to compile and post-process our CSS. Sass compiles our source <code>.scss</code> files into CSS, and Autoprefixer and PostCSS handle browser compatibility. We install the <code>postcss-cli</code> package so we can run PostCSS from the command line."},{"id":"setup--code-3","type":"code","value":"npm i --save-dev autoprefixer postcss postcss-cli sass","language":""}]},{"tag":"li","body":[{"id":"setup--item-4","type":"item","en":"<strong>Install local development tools.</strong> Lastly, to make life a little easier, we recommend installing some dev tools to make running local servers with hot refresh (where changes you make are reflected in the browser automatically) and add some code quality checks."},{"id":"setup--item-5","type":"item","en":"We use <code>nodemon</code> to watch files for changes, <code>npm-run-all</code> to run multiple npm scripts at a time, <code>sirv-cli</code> to run a local server, and <code>stylelint</code> to format CSS like Bootstrap does for consistency."},{"id":"setup--code-4","type":"code","value":"npm i --save-dev nodemon npm-run-all sirv-cli stylelint stylelint-config-twbs-bootstrap","language":""}]}]},{"id":"setup--paragraph-2","type":"paragraph","en":"Now that we have all the necessary dependencies installed, we can get to work creating the project files and importing Bootstrap."},{"id":"project-structure","type":"heading","en":"Project structure","level":2},{"id":"project-structure--paragraph-1","type":"paragraph","en":"We’ve already created the <code>my-project</code> folder and initialized npm. Now we’ll also create our <code>scss</code> folder, stylesheet, and configuration files to round out the project structure. Run the following from <code>my-project</code>, or manually create the folder and file structure shown below."},{"id":"project-structure--code-1","type":"code","value":"mkdir {css,scss}\ntouch index.html scss/styles.scss postcss.config.js stylelint.config.mjs","language":""},{"id":"project-structure--paragraph-2","type":"paragraph","en":"When you’re done, your project should look like this:"},{"id":"project-structure--code-2","type":"code","value":"my-project/\n├── css/\n├── scss/\n│   └── styles.scss\n├── stylelint.config.mjs\n├── index.html\n├── package-lock.json\n├── package.json\n└── postcss.config.js","language":""},{"id":"project-structure--paragraph-3","type":"paragraph","en":"At this point, everything is in the right place, but we’ll need to configure our files and add some npm scripts to compile the CSS."},{"id":"configure-npm","type":"heading","en":"Configure npm","level":2},{"id":"configure-npm--paragraph-1","type":"paragraph","en":"With dependencies installed and our project folder ready for us to start coding, we can now configure our npm scripts and run our project locally."},{"id":"configure-npm--list-1","type":"list","tag":"ol","items":[{"tag":"li","body":[{"id":"configure-npm--item-1","type":"item","en":"<strong>Open <code>postcss.config.js</code> in your editor.</strong> We need to configure Autoprefixer to run after Sass compilation for browser compatibility."},{"id":"configure-npm--code-1","type":"code","value":"const autoprefixer = require('autoprefixer')\n\nmodule.exports = {\n  plugins: [\n    autoprefixer\n  ]\n}","language":""}]},{"tag":"li","body":[{"id":"configure-npm--item-2","type":"item","en":"<strong>Fill in the <code>index.html</code> file.</strong> We need an HTML page to render our project. This page links to the compiled CSS file and includes Bootstrap’s pre-built JavaScript bundle."},{"id":"configure-npm--code-2","type":"code","value":"<!doctype html>\n<html lang=\"en\">\n  <head>\n    <meta charset=\"utf-8\">\n    <meta name=\"viewport\" content=\"width=device-width, initial-scale=1\">\n    <title>Bootstrap w/ npm</title>\n    <link rel=\"stylesheet\" href=\"css/styles.css\">\n  </head>\n  <body>\n    <div class=\"container py-4 px-3 mx-auto\">\n      <h1>Hello, Bootstrap and npm!</h1>\n      <button class=\"btn-solid theme-primary\">Primary button</button>\n    </div>\n    <script type=\"module\" src=\"node_modules/bootstrap/dist/js/bootstrap.bundle.min.js\"></script>\n  </body>\n</html>","language":""},{"id":"configure-npm--item-3","type":"item","en":"We’re including a little bit of Bootstrap styling here with the <code>div class=&quot;container&quot;</code> and <code>&lt;button&gt;</code> so that we see when Bootstrap’s CSS is loaded by our npm scripts. Since this setup doesn’t use a JavaScript bundler, we load Bootstrap’s pre-built JS bundle directly via a <code>&lt;script&gt;</code> tag."},{"id":"configure-npm--item-4","type":"item","en":"<em><a href=\"https://getbootstrap.com/docs/6.0/getting-started/javascript/\">Read our JavaScript docs</a> for more information on how to use Bootstrap’s plugins.</em>"}]},{"tag":"li","body":[{"id":"configure-npm--item-5","type":"item","en":"<strong>Add npm scripts to <code>package.json</code>.</strong> Open <code>package.json</code> and add the following scripts. We use <code>sass</code> to compile our Sass (with <code>--load-path=node_modules</code> so it can resolve Bootstrap), <code>postcss-cli</code> to apply Autoprefixer, <code>nodemon</code> to watch for changes, <code>npm-run-all</code> to run scripts in sequence or in parallel, <code>sirv-cli</code> to serve our project, and <code>stylelint</code> to lint our Sass."},{"id":"configure-npm--code-3","type":"code","value":"{\n  // ...\n  \"scripts\": {\n    \"css-compile\": \"sass --load-path=node_modules --style expanded --source-map --embed-sources scss:css\",\n    \"css-prefix\": \"postcss --config postcss.config.js --replace \\\"css/*.css\\\" \\\"!css/*.min.css\\\"\",\n    \"build\": \"npm-run-all --sequential css-compile css-prefix\",\n    \"watch\": \"nodemon --watch scss/ --ext scss --exec \\\"npm run build\\\"\",\n    \"serve\": \"sirv --port 8080 --dev .\",\n    \"start\": \"npm-run-all build --parallel watch serve\",\n    \"lint\": \"stylelint \\\"scss/**/*.scss\\\"\"\n  },\n  // ...\n}","language":""}]},{"tag":"li","body":[{"id":"configure-npm--item-6","type":"item","en":"<strong>Configure <code>stylelint.config.mjs</code>.</strong> We’re using <code>stylelint-config-twbs-bootstrap</code> to keep our Sass linting consistent with Bootstrap’s own code style."},{"id":"configure-npm--code-4","type":"code","value":"/** @type {import('stylelint').Config} */\nexport default {\n  extends: 'stylelint-config-twbs-bootstrap',\n}","language":""}]},{"tag":"li","body":[{"id":"configure-npm--item-7","type":"item","en":"<strong>And finally, we can start the npm scripts.</strong> From the <code>my-project</code> folder in your terminal, run that newly added npm script:"},{"id":"configure-npm--code-5","type":"code","value":"npm start","language":""}]}]},{"id":"configure-npm--paragraph-2","type":"paragraph","en":"In the next and final section to this guide, we’ll import all of Bootstrap’s CSS."},{"id":"import-bootstrap","type":"heading","en":"Import Bootstrap","level":2},{"id":"import-bootstrap--paragraph-1","type":"paragraph","en":"Importing Bootstrap into our project requires adding a Sass import to our <code>scss/styles.scss</code> file."},{"id":"import-bootstrap--list-1","type":"list","tag":"ol","items":[{"tag":"li","body":[{"id":"import-bootstrap--item-1","type":"item","en":"<strong>Import Bootstrap’s CSS.</strong> Add the following to <code>scss/styles.scss</code> to import all of Bootstrap’s source Sass. We use the <code>@use</code> rule, which is the modern Sass module system."},{"id":"import-bootstrap--code-1","type":"code","value":"// Import all of Bootstrap’s CSS\n@use \"bootstrap/scss/bootstrap\";","language":""},{"id":"import-bootstrap--item-2","type":"item","en":"<em>You can also import our stylesheets individually if you want. <a href=\"https://getbootstrap.com/docs/6.0/customize/sass#importing\">Read our Sass import docs</a> for details.</em>"}]},{"tag":"li","body":[{"id":"import-bootstrap--item-3","type":"item","en":"<strong>Optionally, customize Bootstrap’s Sass tokens.</strong> Since Bootstrap uses Sass modules (<code>@use</code>/<code>@forward</code>), you can override default values using the <code>with ()</code> syntax. You only need to include the keys you want to change — Bootstrap merges your overrides with its defaults."},{"id":"import-bootstrap--code-2","type":"code","value":"@use \"bootstrap/scss/bootstrap\" with (\n  $root-tokens: (\n    --border-radius: .25rem,\n    --spacer: 1.5rem,\n  ),\n  $alert-tokens: (\n    --alert-padding-x: 2rem,\n    --alert-border-radius: 1rem,\n  )\n);","language":""},{"id":"import-bootstrap--item-4","type":"item","en":"<em><a href=\"https://getbootstrap.com/docs/6.0/customize/sass#token-defaults\">Read our Sass customization docs</a> for the full list of available token maps and options.</em>"}]},{"tag":"li","body":[{"id":"import-bootstrap--item-5","type":"item","en":"<strong>And you’re done! 🎉</strong> With Bootstrap’s source Sass fully loaded, your local development server should now look like this:"},{"id":"import-bootstrap--item-6","type":"item","en":"Now you can start adding any Bootstrap components you want to use. Be sure to <a href=\"https://github.com/twbs/examples/tree/main/sass-js\">check out the complete npm Sass and JS example project</a> for how to include additional custom Sass and optimize your build by importing only the parts of Bootstrap’s CSS and JS that you need."}]}]},{"id":"import-bootstrap--paragraph-2","type":"paragraph","en":"<em>See something wrong or out of date here? Please <a href=\"https://github.com/twbs/bootstrap/issues/new/choose\">open an issue on GitHub</a>. Need help troubleshooting? <a href=\"https://github.com/twbs/bootstrap/discussions\">Search or start a discussion</a> on GitHub.</em>"}],"demos":[],"nav":[{"en":"Install","href":"https://getbootstrap.com/docs/6.0/getting-started/install"},{"en":"AI","href":"https://getbootstrap.com/docs/6.0/getting-started/ai"},{"en":"Approach","href":"https://getbootstrap.com/docs/6.0/getting-started/approach"},{"en":"CSS variables","href":"https://getbootstrap.com/docs/6.0/getting-started/css-variables"},{"en":"JavaScript","href":"https://getbootstrap.com/docs/6.0/getting-started/javascript"},{"en":"Browsers & devices","href":"https://getbootstrap.com/docs/6.0/getting-started/browsers-devices"},{"en":"Accessibility","href":"https://getbootstrap.com/docs/6.0/getting-started/accessibility"},{"en":"Quickstart","href":"https://getbootstrap.com/docs/6.0/guides/quickstart"},{"en":"npm","href":"https://getbootstrap.com/docs/6.0/guides/npm"},{"en":"Webpack","href":"https://getbootstrap.com/docs/6.0/guides/webpack"},{"en":"Parcel","href":"https://getbootstrap.com/docs/6.0/guides/parcel"},{"en":"Vite","href":"https://getbootstrap.com/docs/6.0/guides/vite"},{"en":"Contribute","href":"https://getbootstrap.com/d